# See https://docs.github.com/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files for more about ignoring files.
# See https://github.com/github/gitignore - A collection of useful .gitignore templates
# Root .gitignore file

### CUSTOM IGNORES ###
*.venv/
# Matches at any depth (was `*/.env*`, which stopped matching
# project/bash/.env once the Bash implementation moved one directory
# deeper — use **/ so this survives future reorganizations too).
**/.env*
# ...but .env.example templates are meant to be committed.
!**/.env.example
build/
*.egg-info/
*.lock
__pycache__

### TERRAFORM ###
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash*.log
override.tf*
*_override.tf*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!terraform.tfvars.example
*.tfplan
# Note: .terraform.lock.hcl (provider version lock file) is intentionally NOT
# ignored here — it must be committed for reproducible `terraform init` across
# machines/CI. It isn't matched by the `*.lock` rule above (different extension).
